--- a partial SHOW COLUMNS grant hides every column, including the granted one ---
Not enough privileges. To execute this query, it's necessary to have the grant SELECT ON <db>.t_cols. (Missing permissions: SELECT ON <db>.t_cols). (ACCESS_DENIED)
--- granting SHOW COLUMNS on the whole table makes the columns showable ---
Not enough privileges. To execute this query, it's necessary to have the grant SELECT(col_alpha, col_beta) ON <db>.t_cols. (Missing permissions: SELECT(col_beta) ON <db>.t_cols). (ACCESS_DENIED)
--- the database and table of the query are kept ---
Not enough privileges. To execute this query, it's necessary to have the grant SELECT ON <hint_db>.t_hidden. (ACCESS_DENIED)
--- the database name of a CREATE DATABASE is kept ---
Not enough privileges. To execute this query, it's necessary to have the grant CREATE DATABASE ON <no_show_db>.*. (ACCESS_DENIED)
--- a system table names no column either ---
Not enough privileges. To execute this query, it's necessary to have the grant SELECT ON system.clusters. (ACCESS_DENIED)
